  "_skill_md": "---\nname: app-redtrack\ndescription: Internal API for app-redtrack\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://app.redtrack.io\"\n  authMethod: \"Unknown (may need login)\"\n  endpointCount: 23\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# AppRedtrack API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nUnknown (may need login) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (3)\n- `GET /obj/tiktok_web_login_static/tiktok_privacy_protection_framework/config/network.json` — Get TikTok privacy protection network config.\n- `POST /ttwid/check/` — Check the validity of a TTW ID.\n- `POST /v1/user/webid` — Post a web ID for user authentication.\n\n### Data Read (6)\n- `GET /{id}` — Retrieve specific data record by its ID.\n- `GET /api/copilot/dashboards` — Fetch available copilot dashboards.\n- `GET /api/livechat-public/v1/bots/public/bot/{botId}/welcomeMessages` — Get welcome messages for a specific bot.\n- `GET /api/livechat-public/v1/feedback/survey/1` — Get a specific feedback survey.\n- `GET /api/livechat-public/v1/thread/visitor/recent` — Retrieve recent chat threads for a visitor.\n- `GET /v1/lookups/NX-48553e71` — Lookup data associated with a specific ID.\n\n### Data Write (5)\n- `POST /api/10/envelope/` — Send an envelope of data.\n- `POST /api/global-footer/graphql` — Post data to update the global footer.\n- `POST /frontend/observability/page-tracking/store/` — Store page tracking data.\n- `POST /v1/list` — Post data to a list.\n- `POST /wa/` — Post data to the WA endpoint.\n\n### Realtime (1)\n- `GET /livechat-public/v1/message/public` — Receive public live chat messages.\n\n### Config (6)\n- `GET /api/me/settings` — Retrieve user-specific settings.\n- `GET /api/v1/web-cookie-privacy/config` — Get the web cookie privacy configuration.\n- `GET /consentconfig/{consentconfigId}/settings.json` — Get consent configuration settings.\n- `GET /monitor_web/settings/browser-settings` — Get browser-specific monitoring settings.\n- `GET /web-interactives/public/v1/embed/combinedConfigs` — Get combined configurations for web interactives.\n- `POST /service/2/abtest_config/` — Post configuration for A/B testing.\n\n### Core API (2)\n- `GET /api/{apiId}` — Access a core API endpoint by ID.\n- `GET /node-webapp/api/{apiId}` — Access a core API endpoint by ID.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"app-redtrack\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few examples to get you started interacting with the `app-redtrack` API.\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Retrieving user settings.\nasync function getUserSettings() {\n  try {\n    const settings = await client.getApiMeSettings();\n    console.log(\"User Settings:\", settings);\n    return settings;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Failed to retrieve user settings:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Sending an envelope of data.\nasync function sendDataEnvelope(data: any) {\n  try {\n    const response = await client.postApi10Envelope(data);\n    console.log(\"Data Envelope Response:\", response);\n    return response;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Failed to send data envelope:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Retrieving welcome messages for a specific bot.\nasync function getBotWelcomeMessages(botId: string) {\n  try {\n    const messages = await client.getApiLivechatPublicV1BotsPublicBotBotIdWelcomeMessages({ botId });\n    console.log(`Welcome messages for bot ${botId}:`, messages);\n    return messages;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`Failed to retrieve welcome messages for bot ${botId}:`, error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Unknown (may need login)\n**Base URL:** `https://app.redtrack.io`\n**Captured Auth:** 5 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to App Redtrack's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access App Redtrack data without official API access\n- Automate actions on app.redtrack.io (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the App Redtrack frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { AppRedtrackClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await AppRedtrackClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 0 (none)\n- **Session cookies:** 5\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (110)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
